# ── added for the public repo ──
# Everything below is either machine-specific, generated, or not ours to publish.

# Android Studio's project metadata. Some of it is portable, most of it is one
# developer's window layout and caches; publishing the lot invites merge noise.
/.idea/
*.iml

# Gradle and Kotlin build state.
.gradle/
.kotlin/
build/
*/build/

# Signing material. Nothing here should ever exist in the tree, but a rule that
# only matters once is still worth having.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pem
*.pk8
keystore.properties
signing.properties

# Gate artefacts pulled off a device. These come from a real phone and can carry
# real filenames, so they are collected into build/ and never committed.
/build/gates/

# The fixture APK is generated by tools/fixture/build.sh, and the build tree it
# leaves behind is not interesting.
/tools/fixture/build/

# ── working notes, not the app ──
#
# The line is between DESIGN and SCAFFOLDING, not between code and prose.
#
# The design and evidence documents ARE published — PLAN.md, SEARCH.md,
# NEARBY.md, TEMPLATE.md, and the FEATURES / GATES / FIXES ledgers. The README
# claims every assertion is checkable; those files are what make that true, and
# excluding them would leave the claim with nothing behind it.
#
# What stays local is the scaffolding: one machine's setup log, and the notes
# written to brief whoever was working on it next. Neither tells a reader
# anything about the app.
/SETUP.md
/YOUR-CHECKS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/HANDOFF*.md
/*-SPEC.md

# Source art for the launcher icon. The rendered assets ship in app/src/main/res.
/icon/

# Working ledgers for a review round. Scaffolding, not the product.
.unlazy/
